<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Layer-wise shift contributes the largest single-component gain in mean speedup: removing it drops Spd from <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.21\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.21</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.21\times</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.95\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.95</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.95\times</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.41</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.41</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.02</annotation></semantics></math>, since cross-position causal attention alone fails to retain within-block dependence at deeper positions. The drop is heaviest on long-form benchmarks where deeper-position acceptance determines chain length, with Alpaca losing <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.39\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.39</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.39\times</annotation></semantics></math> and MT-Bench <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.32\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.32\times</annotation></semantics></math>, while shorter-answer NQ loses only <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.13\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.13</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.13\times</annotation></semantics></math>. Removing the prefix broadcast costs <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.22\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.22</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.22\times</annotation></semantics></math> as the position queries alone cannot anchor the <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> positions to the verified prefix. The valid-prefix curriculum and rank-guided branching add <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.15\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.15</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.15\times</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.08\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.08</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.08\times</annotation></semantics></math> respectively by preventing wrong-prefix supervision and reallocating verifier budget to uncertain positions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the adaptation side, removing the cost-aware bandit drops mean Spd by <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.10\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.10\times</annotation></semantics></math> while leaving <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged at <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.54</annotation></semantics></math>, since always-update reaches the same accepted length but pays a backward on every query. Removing the head-only action drops mean Spd by <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.24\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.24</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.24\times</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> slightly higher at <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.58</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.58</annotation></semantics></math>, as forcing every triggered update to a full backward gains only <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.04</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.04</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> at the cost of an order-of-magnitude longer backward. The cost-aware bandit and head-only action therefore keep adaptation cheap by skipping weak signals and routing most updates to a backward over only the lm_head and rank head.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we introduce SpecBlock, a block-iterative drafter that produces <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> dependent positions per forward and extends the path through repeated block expansions starting from earlier positions’ hidden states. A layer-wise shift carries each previous position’s hidden state into every decoder layer to preserve within-block dependence, a co-trained rank head sets per-position branching to allocate verifier budget where the drafter is uncertain, and a valid-prefix curriculum masks the loss after the first wrong prediction in the block to prevent wrong prefixes from interfering with training. Beyond static drafting, a cost-aware bandit at deployment uses free verifier feedback to update the drafter selectively, only when the expected throughput gain exceeds the update cost. SpecBlock improves mean speedup over EAGLE-3 by <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13\%</annotation></semantics></math> across three target models, with cost-aware adaptation extending the gain to <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>19</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
