<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Baselines and benchmarks</h3>

<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare against six drafting baselines.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard speculative sampling
(SpS)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> samples a
chain of future tokens autoregressively from a smaller
off-the-shelf drafter and lets the target verify the chain in
one parallel forward. We pair Llama-3.1-8B with Llama-3.2-1B,
and the Qwen3 targets with Qwen3-0.6B.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Medusa</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> attaches <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent
decoding heads at fixed offsets to the target’s last hidden
state, with no cross-position attention or layer-wise
dependence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ParallelSpec</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> predicts <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>
future tokens in one drafter forward by appending <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> learnable
<span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> tokens after the prefix and reading their
last-layer hidden states, under a group-wise causal mask that
blocks attention from <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span>s in earlier parallel
groups.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Falcon</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> is the closest blockwise
prior work. It drafts semi-autoregressive blocks of <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tokens
with a hybrid drafter combining LSTM layers with
relaxed-causal-mask self-attention, letting positions inside
the same <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{\times}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{\times}k</annotation></semantics></math> block attend to one another, and verifies
through a custom-designed static decoding tree.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EAGLE-3</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> is an autoregressive
token-level drafter that fuses the target’s low-, mid-, and
high-level hidden states as input, replacing the top-layer-only
reuse of EAGLE-1/2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, and grows
a dynamic draft tree depth by depth by calling the drafter
once per added depth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SpecBlock+OSD</span> instantiates Online Speculative
Decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> on the SpecBlock drafter as the
always-update baseline. Rejection-position pairs of the draft
and target distributions are logged to a replay buffer, and the
drafter is updated every eight queries via forward-KL
distillation, with no bandit gating over which signals to
apply.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benchmarks.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The six benchmarks vary substantially in prompt count, from <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> multi-turn
dialogues in MT-Bench and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="164" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>164</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">164</annotation></semantics></math> code prompts in HumanEval, through <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math>
competition problems in MATH-500 and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="549" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>549</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">549</annotation></semantics></math> translation pairs in WMT-23, up
to <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> instruction prompts in Alpaca and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{,}610" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,610</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{,}610</annotation></semantics></math> open-domain
questions in Natural Questions. Each prompt is rendered through the
target’s official chat template, with thinking mode disabled for Qwen3 so
the verifier output is comparable to Llama, and passed once through the
speculative decoding loop under greedy decoding (<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}0</annotation></semantics></math>) or stochastic
decoding (<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math>). Generation is capped at <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}024</annotation></semantics></math> newly committed
tokens. We report speedup as the wall-clock ratio over vanilla
autoregressive decoding on the same prompt set, accepted length <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as
the average length committed per verifier call, and drafting cost
<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathcal{D}}\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathcal{D}}\%</annotation></semantics></math> as the share of per-iteration latency spent on drafter
forwards. Cost-aware adaptation is reported only on MATH-500, Alpaca, NQ,
and WMT-23, whose streaming-prompt counts are large enough for the
adaptation backward to amortize its cost; HumanEval and MT-Bench leave too
little traffic for the bandit’s value estimates to converge.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Inference procedure</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.5 Inference procedure ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> traces one verifier iteration of SpecBlock.
The drafter is invoked at most <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> times to grow a tree of up to <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{\cdot}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{\cdot}K</annotation></semantics></math>
depth, the verifier scores all candidates in a single parallel forward, and
the longest accepted prefix is committed before the next iteration starts.
The first block conditions on the target’s multi-layer features at the
prefix-end position, while later blocks condition on the drafter’s own
cached last-layer state at the starting position, bypassing the projection
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Per-position branching width follows the rank head’s
bucket through the map <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. We recommend two configurations of
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> over the four buckets defined in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Rank-guided tree expansion ‣ 3 SpecBlock ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>:
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,4,10,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,4,10,0]</annotation></semantics></math>, which concentrates tree budget on the less confident
buckets where the target token sits deeper and gives up on the rank<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>10 bucket, and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,4,6,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,4,6,4]</annotation></semantics></math>, which
trims the wide rank-<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> bucket and keeps a <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-candidate fallback at
give-up positions for out-of-distribution traffic.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> SpecBlock inference, one verifier iteration.</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            target <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, drafter <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, last verified token <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and multi-layer features <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h^{\text{low}}_{t},h^{\text{mid}}_{t},h^{\text{top}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>mid</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>top</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h^{\text{low}}_{t},h^{\text{mid}}_{t},h^{\text{top}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>’s most recent forward, block depth <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, block budget <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, bucket-to-branching map <math id="alg2.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            tokens committed in this iteration

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}\leftarrow W_{\text{cond}}\,[h^{\text{low}}_{t},h^{\text{mid}}_{t},h^{\text{top}}_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>mid</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>top</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}\leftarrow W_{\text{cond}}\,[h^{\text{low}}_{t},h^{\text{mid}}_{t},h^{\text{top}}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{starts}\leftarrow\{(c_{t},\,\mathrm{embed}(x_{t}))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>starts</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>embed</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{starts}\leftarrow\{(c_{t},\,\mathrm{embed}(x_{t}))\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> first-block starting point uses target features
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tree}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tree</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tree}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> empty draft tree rooted at <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i,k},\,h^{(L)}_{i,k},\,\mathrm{bkt}_{i,k}\}_{i,\,k=1}^{K}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\theta}(\mathrm{starts})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>bkt</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>starts</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i,k},\,h^{(L)}_{i,k},\,\mathrm{bkt}_{i,k}\}_{i,\,k=1}^{K}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\theta}(\mathrm{starts})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> batched forward, <math id="alg2.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> positions per starting point
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each starting point <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and each position <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               attach the top-<math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\mathrm{bkt}_{i,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>bkt</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\mathrm{bkt}_{i,k})</annotation></semantics></math> tokens of <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tree}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>tree</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tree}</annotation></semantics></math> as candidates at position <math id="alg2.l9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{starts}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>starts</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{starts}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> next-block starting points selected by the rank head, each carrying its cached <math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(L)}_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(L)}_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> and sampled token

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{prefix},\,\mathrm{bonus})\leftarrow\mathcal{M}.\mathrm{verify}(\mathrm{tree})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>prefix</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>bonus</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>verify</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>tree</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{prefix},\,\mathrm{bonus})\leftarrow\mathcal{M}.\mathrm{verify}(\mathrm{tree})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> single parallel target forward
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{prefix}\,\cup\,\mathrm{bonus}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>prefix</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">∪</mo><mi>bonus</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{prefix}\,\cup\,\mathrm{bonus}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Rank head</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Distribution summary features.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Rank-guided tree expansion ‣ 3 SpecBlock ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> states that the rank head reads a
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional summary <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(p_{t,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(p_{t,k})</annotation></semantics></math> of the draft distribution
alongside the hidden state. We detail those <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> dimensions here. The
summary captures how peaky or flat the distribution is through three
kinds of signal. The bulk of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> records the log-probability profile
of the top-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, which describes how mass spreads across the
most likely candidates and contributes ten dimensions. Three further
dimensions capture the logit gaps between the top token and its
rank-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, rank-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, and rank-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> competitors, telling the rank head how
distinguishable the leader is from close runners-up. The remaining two
dimensions are scalar summaries: the probability of the top token, and
the entropy of the distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Classification quality.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The rank head is supervised as a four-way classifier over the bucket
labels defined in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Rank-guided tree expansion ‣ 3 SpecBlock ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and its classification quality
directly affects how the verifier budget is spent. We evaluate it as a
standalone classifier on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 72{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>72,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 72{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> validation positions of the
SpecBlock drafter for Llama-3.1-8B, restricted to positions whose
valid-prefix mask is one. At each such position we record the predicted
bucket and the ground-truth bucket derived from the target token’s rank
within <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Classification quality. ‣ Appendix B Rank head ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports per-bucket precision, recall, and
F1 together with class frequency. The class frequencies are sharply
imbalanced, with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> accounting for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="75.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>75.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">75.2\%</annotation></semantics></math> of positions while <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> each fall under <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\%</annotation></semantics></math>. The two extreme buckets are the
easiest to classify. The confident bucket <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches precision
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.978" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.978</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.978</annotation></semantics></math> since the drafter is well-calibrated when the target sits at
rank <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the give-up bucket <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches F1 <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.822" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.822</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.822</annotation></semantics></math> since
high-rank positions carry clear distribution-shape signals such as flat
or multi-modal <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The two middle buckets <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are
the hardest, with F1 around <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.46" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.46</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.46</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, and most errors fall
between the two adjacent buckets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Rank head classification quality on <math id="A2.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 72{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>72,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 72{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> held-out positions of the SpecBlock drafter for Llama-3.1-8B.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
