<td id="A2.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">5.7</td>
<td id="A2.T3.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.854</td>
<td id="A2.T3.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.792</td>
<td id="A2.T3.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.822</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Per-position acceptance rate</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure two acceptance-rate diagnostics averaged across benchmarks.
<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that the drafter’s greedy token at chain
position <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> matches the target’s greedy continuation, assuming
positions <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\ldots,k{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\ldots,k{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> have all already matched, swept over
<math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\ldots,K{\cdot}M{=}8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\ldots,K{\cdot}M{=}8</annotation></semantics></math> across two cross-block iterations. The chain
position <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> does not correspond to a fixed block-internal index, since
the boundary depends on how many positions of block 0 are taken before
block 1 starts. <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{m,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m,j}</annotation></semantics></math> replots the rate at position <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> of
block <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> under the same prior-match filter, with block 1 additionally
assuming block 0 was fully accepted.</p>
</div>
