<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Case study response with per-token acceptance shading.
<span id="A5.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#D2F0D7;">green token</span> indicates a
token drafted by the drafter and accepted by the verifier;
<span id="A5.F6.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCDCD;">red token</span> indicates a
bonus token sampled from the target after acceptance. Each response is
shown for the first 30 committed tokens, with a trailing <math id="A5.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>
marking the omitted tail.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix E Case Study ‣ SpecBlock: Block-Iterative Speculative Decoding with Dynamic Tree Drafting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> visualizes the iter-<math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> draft tree of each drafter on the same prompt; node coloring shows which drafter forward produced each token. EAGLE-3 grows depth-by-depth, so reaching depth <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> costs seven sequential drafter forwards, with each forward shown in a different color, fwd <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> through fwd <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>. SpecBlock pays only two forwards on the same prompt: block-<math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> emits all <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}4</annotation></semantics></math> chain positions in one forward drawn horizontally, and block-<math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> then batches additional chains from rank-head–selected starts; the two blocks are colored differently. Both drafters land on the same accepted prefix <span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">F ib onacci Sequence</span>. EAGLE-3 keeps drafting and the verifier walks three more depths, committing eight tokens including a bonus over seven forwards. SpecBlock stops at the block-<math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> chain and commits five tokens including a bonus over two forwards. The case makes the SpecBlock trade-off visible: SpecBlock trades a slightly shorter accepted run per iteration for an iteration that finishes in two drafter calls instead of seven.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
